{"type":"AcceptanceSupplierContext","objective":"Provide a protected executable oracle for readablePaths confinement. The oracle must distinguish correct root traversal and per-file filtering from private-name, matching-line, or byte disclosure, and it must cover directory admission, exact-file admission, direct reads, and unrestricted compatibility.","command":"node --test union-acceptance/readable-paths-protected.test.mjs","artifactPath":"union-acceptance/readable-paths-protected.test.mjs","testVectors":[{"id":"omitted-root-traversal","given":["public/match.txt and private/secret.txt contain the same token needle","readablePaths is [public]"],"when":"list_files and search run with path omitted","then":["both observations succeed","list and hits contain public/match.txt"],"forbidden":["private/secret.txt","the private matching line","a root-base refusal"]},{"id":"dot-root-traversal","given":["the same mixed public/private fixture","readablePaths is [public]"],"when":"list_files and search run with path dot","then":["dot is accepted as root traversal","list and hits contain only admitted descendants"],"forbidden":["private filenames","private matching lines","private bytes"]},{"id":"directory-and-file-admission","given":["public/a.txt and public/nested/b.txt exist with searchable tokens","one toolset admits public and another admits exact file public/a.txt"],"when":"list_files, search, and direct read exercise both toolsets","then":["directory admission exposes and reads both descendants","exact-file admission exposes, searches, and reads only public/a.txt","direct read rejects public/nested/b.txt under exact-file admission"],"forbidden":["exact-file admission exposing a sibling, descendant, or ancestor"]},{"id":"explicit-private-base-refusal","given":["private/secret.txt exists and contains token needle","readablePaths is [public]"],"when":"list_files and search use explicit base private","then":["both return structured JSON errors stating only that the path is outside declared readable scope"],"forbidden":["the word private","secret.txt","needle","protected content","files or hits payloads"]},{"id":"unrestricted-compatibility","given":["public and private files exist","one toolset omits readablePaths and another supplies an empty array"],"when":"list_files, search, and direct read execute through both toolsets","then":["both toolsets preserve unrestricted behavior for all three operations"],"forbidden":["deny-all behavior","different behavior between omitted and empty readablePaths"]}],"constraints":["The current authoritative test is a witnessed weak incumbent: use it only as evidence of omissions, not as a template to preserve.","Every vector must be a separately named Node test using its exact vector id.","Use one fresh mkdtempSync fixture per test and t.after cleanup with rmSync.","For list and search refusals, assert the response has an error and lacks files and hits; assert its serialized bytes omit private, secret.txt, the matching token, and protected content.","Do not use Date.now, Math.random, environment variables, network APIs, child processes, timers, sleeps, or dynamic imports."],"priorReviewResidue":{"transportHistory":"Two free-Gemini rounds returned schema-valid but incomplete artifacts. The first Claude escalation produced no artifact because the live outer harness bound killed its 300-second provider-local exchange after 180 seconds. The runtime bound is now aligned at 330 seconds; this is one transport retry, not a new capability escalation.","instruction":"Return the complete artifact. It is incomplete unless its executable source contains every required call and assertion in this exact matrix.","omitted-root-traversal":{"requiredCalls":["list_files with omitted path","search with omitted path"],"requiredAssertions":["public list member","exactly one public search hit","no error","serialized list and hits omit private filename, token, and bytes"]},"dot-root-traversal":{"requiredCalls":["list_files with path dot","search with path dot"],"requiredAssertions":["public list member","exactly one public search hit","no error","serialized list and hits omit private filename, token, and bytes"]},"directory-and-file-admission":{"requiredCalls":["directory list_files","directory search","directory read a.txt","directory read nested/b.txt","exact-file list_files from root","exact-file search from root","exact-file read a.txt","exact-file rejected read nested/b.txt"],"requiredAssertions":["directory sees both descendants","exact-file sees only a.txt","rejected direct read has error and no text/path payload"]},"explicit-private-base-refusal":{"requiredCalls":["list_files with path private","search with path private"],"requiredAssertions":["both are error-only objects","neither has files or hits","both serialized objects omit private, secret.txt, needle, and protected bytes"]},"unrestricted-compatibility":{"requiredCalls":["omitted-scope list_files, search, and direct read","empty-scope list_files, search, and direct read"],"requiredAssertions":["both modes see the same public and private files","both modes return the same public and private search hits","both modes read private bytes"]}},"evidence":[{"path":"src/agent-tools.mjs","text":"import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
import { existsSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { dirname, relative, resolve, sep } from "node:path";
import { mkdirSync } from "node:fs";
import { applyEditBlocks } from "./edits.mjs";
import { runTestsCommand } from "./executor.mjs";

const SKIP = new Set([".git", "node_modules", ".lake", "dist", "coverage"]);

function inside(root, requested = ".") {
  const path = resolve(root, requested);
  if (path !== resolve(root) && !path.startsWith(resolve(root) + sep)) throw new Error("path escapes the admitted territory");
  return path;
}

function walk(root, at = root, out = [], max = 600) {
  if (out.length >= max || !existsSync(at)) return out;
  for (const entry of readdirSync(at, { withFileTypes: true })) {
    if (out.length >= max || SKIP.has(entry.name)) continue;
    const path = resolve(at, entry.name);
    if (entry.isDirectory()) walk(root, path, out, max);
    else if (entry.isFile()) out.push(relative(root, path));
  }
  return out;
}

export function digest(bytes) {
  return createHash("sha256").update(bytes).digest("hex");
}

export function territorySnapshot(root, { maxFiles = 600 } = {}) {
  const files = walk(root, root, [], maxFiles);
  return { files, truncated: files.length >= maxFiles };
}

export function createAgentTools({ root, verifyCommand, acceptanceCommand = verifyCommand, commands = {}, writablePaths = [], readablePaths = [], maxObservationBytes = 10000 } = {}) {
  const changed = new Map();
  const admittedWrites = writablePaths.map((path) => relative(root, inside(root, path)));
  const writeAdmitted = (path) => !admittedWrites.length || admittedWrites.some((allowed) => path === allowed || path.startsWith(`${allowed}${sep}`));
  const admittedReads = readablePaths.map((path) => relative(root, inside(root, path)));
  const readAdmitted = (path) => !admittedReads.length || admittedReads.some((allowed) => path === allowed || path.startsWith(`${allowed}${sep}`));
  const observe = (value) => JSON.stringify(value).slice(0, maxObservationBytes);
  const checkObservation = (result) => ({ passed: result.passed, output: result.passed ? "exit=0" : result.output.slice(-8000) });
  const checks = () => {
    const verification = runTestsCommand(root, verifyCommand);
    const acceptance = acceptanceCommand === verifyCommand ? verification : runTestsCommand(root, acceptanceCommand);
    return { verification, acceptance };
  };
  return {
    changed,
    execute(action) {
      const args = action?.args || {};
      if (action.action === "list_files") {
        const relativePath = relative(root, resolve(root, args.path || "."));
        if (relativePath !== "" && !readAdmitted(relativePath)) return observe({ error: `list_files path is outside declared readable paths: ${relativePath}` });
        const base = inside(root, args.path || ".");
        return observe({ files: walk(root, base, [], Math.min(Number(args.max) || 250, 600)).filter(file => readAdmitted(file)) });
      }
      if (action.action === "search") {
        const query = String(args.query || "");
        if (!query) return observe({ error: "search requires args.query" });
        const relativePath = relative(root, resolve(root, args.path || "."));
        if (relativePath !== "" && !readAdmitted(relativePath)) return observe({ error: `search path is outside declared readable paths: ${relativePath}` });
        const base = inside(root, args.path || ".");
        const hits = [];
        for (const file of walk(root, base, [], 600)) {
          if (!readAdmitted(file)) continue;
          const path = inside(root, file);
          let text;
          try { text = readFileSync(path, "utf8"); } catch { continue; }
          for (const [index, line] of text.split("\n").entries()) {
            if (line.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase())) hits.push({ path: file, line: index + 1, text: line.slice(0, 500) });
            if (hits.length >= 80) return observe({ hits, truncated: true });
          }
        }
        return observe({ hits, truncated: false });
      }
      if (action.action === "read") {
        const path = inside(root, args.path);
        const relativePath = relative(root, path);
        if (!readAdmitted(relativePath)) return observe({ ok: false, error: `read path is outside declared readable paths: ${relativePath}` });
        const start = Math.max(1, Number(args.startLine) || 1), end = Math.min(start + 399, Number(args.endLine) || start + 199);
        const lines = readFileSync(path, "utf8").split("\n");
        return observe({ path: relativePath, startLine: start, endLine: Math.min(end, lines.length), text: lines.slice(start - 1, end).join("\n") });
      }
      if (action.action === "edit") {
        const path = inside(root, args.path), relativePath = relative(root, path);
        if (!writeAdmitted(relativePath)) return observe({ ok: false, error: `edit path is outside declared writable paths: ${relativePath}`, writablePaths: admittedWrites });
        const existed = existsSync(path);
        const before = existed ? readFileSync(path, "utf8") : "";
        const blocks = (() => {
          if (typeof args.blocks === "string") return args.blocks;
          if (Array.isArray(args.blocks)) return args.blocks.map((block) => {
            if (typeof block === "string") return block;
            if (block && typeof block.search === "string" && typeof block.replace === "string") return `<<<<<<< SEARCH\n${block.search}\n=======\n${block.replace}\n>>>>>>> REPLACE`;
            return "";
          }).filter(Boolean).join("\n");
          if (args.blocks && typeof args.blocks.search === "string" && typeof args.blocks.replace === "string") return `<<<<<<< SEARCH\n${args.blocks.search}\n=======\n${args.blocks.replace}\n>>>>>>> REPLACE`;
          return "";
        })();
        const result = applyEditBlocks(before, blocks);
        if (!result.ok) return observe({ ok: false, error: result.reason || "no edit blocks" });
        if (!changed.has(relativePath)) changed.set(relativePath, { existed, bytes: Buffer.from(before), digest: digest(before) });
        mkdirSync(dirname(path), { recursive: true });
        writeFileSync(path, result.result);
        const { verification, acceptance } = checks();
        return observe({ ok: true, editBlocks: result.count, verification: checkObservation(verification), acceptance: checkObservation(acceptance) });
      }
      if (action.action === "command") {
        const named = commands[String(args.name || "")];
        if (!named?.command) return observe({ error: `command is not admitted: ${args.name || "(missing)"}`, available: Object.keys(commands) });
        const result = runTestsCommand(root, named.command, { timeoutMs: named.timeoutMs || 120000 });
        return observe({ command: args.name, passed: result.passed, output: result.output });
      }
      if (action.action === "test" || action.action === "finish") {
        const { verification, acceptance } = checks();
        return observe({ verification: checkObservation(verification), acceptance: checkObservation(acceptance), changedPaths: [...changed.keys()] });
      }
      return observe({ error: `unknown action ${action?.action}` });
    },
    verify() { return checks(); },
    changes() {
      return [...changed.entries()].map(([path, before]) => {
        const current = readFileSync(inside(root, path));
        return { path, before, after: current, afterDigest: digest(current), changedBytes: Math.abs(current.length - before.bytes.length) + current.length };
      });
    },
  };
}
"}],"contract":["Return one complete Node test artifact. Every test vector id must be the exact test name so host TAP output witnesses execution.","Exercise every given/when/then/forbidden clause with concrete assertions. A comment or title alone is not coverage.","The artifact must fail against the supplied incumbent because of behavioral assertions, not syntax, import, fixture, or infrastructure errors.","Use mkdtempSync and test cleanup. Do not use network, child processes, environment variables, dynamic imports, clocks, randomness, timers, or sleeps.","Import implementation APIs using paths relative to the declared artifactPath. Do not alter implementation source."]}
